<title>GERMANY: BASF does not expect record return in 1997.</title>
<headline>BASF does not expect record return in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group BASF AG said on Wednesday it did not expect to reach the record levels of return on capital reported for 1988 and 1989 in the 1997 year.</p>
<p>&quot;We will probably not be able to beat the record levels of 1988 and 1989,&quot; the company's management board chairman Juergen Strube told a news conference.</p>
<p>BASF recorded a return on capital of 13.1 percent in 1988 and 14.2 percent in 1989. It is expecting to report a yield of around 11.2 percent for the current year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
